Griaß di Mail is an independent downstream of Convey 51.0, itself
derived from Geary. Original authorship, copyright and notices are retained
in individual files, AUTHORS, THANKS and the original Git history.

This elected application source copy and the new debian/ packaging are licensed
under GNU GPL version 3 only. See COPYING and docs/release/GPLV3-COPY.md.
On Debian/Ubuntu, the complete GPLv3 text is also available at
/usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3.

This is not a blanket licence for every file. The repository's
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md, COPYING.icons, COPYING.sounds and docs/licenses/ retain
component-specific copyright notices and licence texts. These are installed
under /usr/share/licenses/io.github.d3rpapah0d3n.GriabuntuMail/ by the application build.
The original LGPL reference is preserved as COPYING.LGPL-2.1-original.
In particular, bundled Dark Reader is MIT, ValaUnit remains LGPL, the Snowball
binding retains its BSD notice, and icon/sound/brand assets retain their
individual CC, LGPL, GPL or public-domain terms. System libraries are separate Ubuntu packages;
their notices are available in their respective /usr/share/doc directories.

The current distribution inventory and original/adaptation credits are in
ARTWORK-INVENTORY.md, COPYING.icons and COPYING.sounds, with original GNOME,
CC and LGPL notices/texts installed. This is a development preview, not a legal
warranty or an acceptance claim for personal accounts. See release evidence and
the corresponding-source locations supplied beside each binary download.

The original app/tray icon and banner were generated by the owner, Markus Kainer,
using ChatGPT with text-only prompts and no supplied third-party inputs.
They are preserved in design/owner-artwork-20261027/ with original SHA-256 hashes.
This provenance is not a claim of exclusive human authorship or trademark clearance.
The owner authorised their inclusion in this fork and its packages. No old CC0
study's licence is asserted for these separately supplied originals. See the
installed Griabuntu-Mail-Artwork.md and docs/ARTWORK-PROVENANCE.md.
Older source-history artwork keeps its own terms.

The active Griaß di Mail banner is a documented AI-edited derivative of that
owner-supplied original. The original icon bytes and all six original hashes
remain intact; full provenance accompanies the package. The exact 23 installed
action-icon paths and hashes are provided in ARTWORK-PATHS.json. Original
per-work CC licences remain applicable and are not blanketed by app GPL terms.
